{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "52", "x": 0.9038164196379167, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.02992682896571904, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "READING PASSAGE 2", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.16345827991355463, "w": 0.2545169675210174, "h": 0.02039118517446672, "c": 1, "size": 14.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "You should spend about 20 minutes on Question 14- 26, which are based on", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.20380311983075466, "w": 0.8272700844590317, "h": 0.02039118517446672, "c": 1, "size": 14.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Reading Passage 2 below", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2343584285207526, "w": 0.27628452745684906, "h": 0.02039118517446672, "c": 1, "size": 14.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Procrastination", "x": 0.4062521049654578, "y": 0.27483674558535226, "w": 0.23020891612361763, "h": 0.026142565890596797, "c": 1, "size": 18.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "A psychologist explains why we put off important tasks and how we can break", "x": 0.12138681557801057, "y": 0.32391797317224386, "w": 0.7981029013229103, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "this habit", "x": 0.47075521828946754, "y": 0.3522483232463815, "w": 0.09986104793010833, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "A", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.39051660050585896, "w": 0.02121427120700475, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Procrastination is the habit of delaying a necessary task, usually by focusing", "x": 0.16774843308549978, "y": 0.39051660050585896, "w": 0.7658836784682116, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "on less urgent, more enjoyable, and easier activities instead. We all do it from time", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4188469505799966, "w": 0.8266082858822216, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "to time. We might be composing a message to a friend who we have to let down,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4471773383755267, "w": 0.8260336335161456, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "or putting together an important report for college or work; we're doing our best", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.47553239596175895, "w": 0.8261206772019258, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "to avoid doing the job at hand, but deep down we know that we should just be", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5037144632419364, "w": 0.8266171030282488, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "getting on with it. Unfortunately, berating ourselves won't stop us procrastinating", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.532044813316074, "w": 0.8263818082592668, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "again. In fact, it's one of the worst things we can do. This matters because, as my", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5603752011116042, "w": 0.8256633133830026, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "research shows, procrastination doesn't just waste time, but is actually linked to", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5887055889071343, "w": 0.8266635468323223, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "other problems, too.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.617035938981272, "w": 0.20952642903637925, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "B", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6553041785193569, "w": 0.020206412464245704, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Contrary to popular belief, procrastination is not due to laziness or poor time", "x": 0.16774843308549978, "y": 0.6553041785193569, "w": 0.7658836784682116, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "management. Scientific studies suggest procrastination is, in fact, caused by poor", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6836716464437252, "w": 0.826011898225939, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "mood management. This makes sense if we consider that people are more likely", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7120019965178628, "w": 0.8265347754903435, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "to put off starting or completing tasks that they are really not keen to do. If just", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7403324220347854, "w": 0.8259249570651125, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "thinking about the task threatens our sense of self-worth or makes us anxious, we", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7686627721089231, "w": 0.8266638544071838, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "will be more likely to put it off. Research involving brain imaging has found that", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7969931221830607, "w": 0.8266554473609719, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "areas of the brain linked to detection of threats and emotion regulation are", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8251751517418456, "w": 0.8260336335161456, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "actually different in people who chronically procrastinate compared to those who", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8535055018159833, "w": 0.8263600729690601, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "don't procrastinate frequently.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.881860672566393, "w": 0.31656130177164143, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}